[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver.py: Implemented interface data types, ComparatorOp, and protocol declarations with concrete Version/VersionRange formatting and dataclass exceptions
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Implemented SemVer 2.0 parser/comparator, range algebra (comparators, caret, tilde, wildcards, hyphen, unions, prerelease rules), repository indexing, and MRV backtracking dependency resolver with conflict reporting
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: Author unit tests for semver_solver_impl singletons: VersionEngine parsing/precedence/range semantics including leading-zero, grammar, trimming, comparator/prefix/wildcard/hyphen/union, and prerelease targeting branches; PackageRepository descending ordering, shallow-copy, dependencies, and PackageNotFoundError; DependencySolver highest-compatible selection, multi-root intersection, backtracking, empty root, and ResolutionConflictError for unsatisfiable and unregistered packages with structured conflict attributes.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: In semver_solver_impl.py lines 280-284 (_compile_range), parse_range strips the caller's text into raw_range before validation, so when the input contains only whitespace the raised InvalidRangeError carries the stripped empty string (raw_range='') rather than the original text (e.g. '   '). semver_solver.pyi defines InvalidRangeError.raw_range as the Original malformed range expression string, and semver_solver_impl.pyi's parse_range must raise InvalidRangeError for whitespace-only input while preserving that payload; expected postcondition is that raw_range equals the caller's original, untrimmed input exactly. The author's CHANGE implemented trimming on the input and reused the trimmed value for error construction, so the error payload no longer reflects the original range text. Retain the untrimmed input when constructing InvalidRangeError while still trimming only the VersionRange result.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Fixed parse_range feedback: _compile_range now validates the caller's untrimmed text and constructs InvalidRangeError.raw_range from it verbatim (including whitespace-only input), while parse_range trims only the accepted VersionRange.raw_text; audited sibling exception payloads (InvalidVersionError, PackageNotFoundError) to confirm they preserve original inputs.
