[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: The recent change only adjusted how the untrimmed raw-range payload is preserved and did not add assertions for the grammar or error branches that remain uncovered, so the contracted postconditions are still unverified. parse_range must parse and normalize the unbounded wildcard forms ('*', 'x', 'X'), yet no assertion parses a bare wildcard. Caret expansion around the first non-zero component is unasserted for a major-zero operand whose minor is an unspecified wildcard, for a major-zero and minor-zero operand whose patch is an unspecified wildcard, and for a major-zero and minor-zero operand with a concrete patch, so the zero-major caret upper boundaries are never checked. Tilde expansion is unasserted for an operand that leaves the minor an unspecified wildcard. Relational comparators combined with wildcard operands ('>', '>=', '<', '<=' with M.x or M.m.x) are unasserted, including the normalization that turns a relational comparison against a wildcard block into an inequality at the next block boundary. The wildcard form of the '!=' comparator is unasserted, including the bounded-block branch that excludes an entire minor or patch block. Hyphen ranges whose upper operand is a wildcard are unasserted even though the grammar accepts wildcard operands after operators. The reachable InvalidRangeError conditions contracted for malformed range text are also unasserted: an unbounded wildcard supplied as either hyphen-range operand, '!=', '>' or '<' combined with an unbounded wildcard, caret and tilde combined with an unbounded wildcard, a hyphen clause that does not have the LOW - HIGH shape, and an operator token with a missing operand; each violates the contracted range syntax and must raise InvalidRangeError carrying the original range text. Finally, resolve must merge a candidate release's transitive dependencies into the accumulated constraint mapping and restore that mapping when the search backtracks, and must report every requesting package involved in a conflict rather than only the dependency target; no assertion drives a resolution in which a newly introduced transitive constraint is later rolled back, nor one in which a transitive requester appears in the reported conflicting packages.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: Add the grammar/error and expansion assertions the feedback identified as uncovered: (1) parse_range now asserts bare unbounded wildcards '*'/'x'/'X' parse, and InvalidRangeError for unbounded wildcards as either hyphen operand, '!=*' / '>*' / '<*', '^*' / '~*', non-LOW-HIGH hyphen clauses, and operator tokens missing operands (all asserting raw_range carries the original text); (2) satisfies now covers zero-major caret upper boundaries (^0.x, ^0.0.x, ^0.0.3), wildcard-minor carets/tildes (^1.x, ~1.x, ~1.2.x, ~0.x), relational comparators against wildcard blocks (>, >=, <, <= with M.x and M.m.x normalizing to the next block boundary), wildcard '!=' block exclusion (!=1.x, !=1.2.x), and hyphen ranges with wildcard upper operands (1.2.3 - 2.x, 1.2.3 - 2.3.x); (3) DependencySolver now drives a branch whose newly merged transitive constraint (q >=1.0.0 from p 2.0.0) must be rolled back before p 1.0.0 succeeds with q 0.5.0, and asserts a transitive requester ('b') appears alongside the dependency target ('c') in ResolutionConflictError.conflicting_packages.
