[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: The latest change to malformed-range payload construction did not touch the statements that remain uncovered, and after the companion suite was updated these seven spans persist because no conforming public call can execute them. The unbounded-operand guard in the caret boundary expansion (line 144) and the corresponding guard in the tilde boundary expansion (line 160) duplicate the caller's unbounded-wildcard rejection, so the operand's major component is always defined when those helpers are invoked and both raises are unreachable. The missing-operand guard in the single-atom compiler (line 176) cannot fire because a clause token that exactly equals an operator is always paired with the following token, and any other operator-prefixed token leaves a non-empty remainder. The empty-comparator acceptance at line 202 is only reachable when an unbounded wildcard is supplied as a relational operand, a form the contracted wildcard grammar does not admit because contracted unbounded wildcards are standalone '*', 'x', and 'X' operands and every other operator applied to an unbounded wildcard is malformed range syntax, so this degenerate no-op acceptance is an uncontracted caller assumption rather than contracted behavior. The unsupported-operator fallthrough (line 236) is unreachable because every operator recognized by the clause tokenizer is consumed by an earlier branch, and the empty-clause guard (line 243) is unreachable because the range compiler rejects empty union clauses before dispatching and strips each clause. The empty-conflict-trail fallback explanation in resolve (line 642) is unreachable because every failing search path records at least one conflict derivation before returning failure. Prune these dead or uncontracted statements, or annotate them with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: <reason>)'.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Addressed coverage feedback: pruned the unreachable missing-operand guard in _compile_atom, the redundant empty-clause guard in _compile_clause, and the dead empty-conflict-trail fallback in resolve; removed the uncontracted relational unbounded-wildcard no-op acceptance so '>=*', '>*', '<*', '<=*' are rejected as malformed range syntax via the bounded-operand guard; annotated the caret/tilde operand-boundary guards and the unsupported-operator fallthrough with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: ...)' where static typing/invariants require them.
